---
import { Code } from 'astro-expressive-code/components';
import Aside from '@/components/mdx/Aside.astro';

const flowSnippet = `import { expect, test } from './blackbox-testbed';

test.describe('Customer checkout', { tag: '@flow:checkout-flow' }, () => {
  test('creates an order without refunding', async ({ capture, request }) => {
    const response = await request.post('/checkout', {
      data: { cartId: 'cart-123', paymentMethodId: 'pm_card_visa' },
    });

    expect(response.status()).toBe(201);
    await expect(capture).toMatchCatalog();
  });
});`;

const effectsSnippet = `specVersion: "0.1"
flow: checkout-flow
requires:
  - { boundary: postgres, op: INSERT, key: orders }
forbids:
  - { boundary: http, op: POST, key: /refunds }`;

const verifyCommand = `pnpm exec blackbox verify --flow checkout-flow --json`;

const verifyOutput = `{
  "command": "verify",
  "status": "passed",
  "data": {
    "flowIds": ["checkout-flow"],
    "layers": {
      "test": { "state": "passed", "verdict": "passed" },
      "effects": { "state": "passed", "verdict": "satisfied" }
    }
  }
}`;

const featureCommands = `pnpm exec blackbox status --json
pnpm exec blackbox requirements validate 'requirements/**/*.ears' --json
pnpm exec blackbox features check --features ./features --json
pnpm exec blackbox verify --flow subscribe-unknown-user --json`;
---

<section class="bb-quickstart" id="quickstart-track">
  <div class="bb-track-pick" aria-label="Quickstart shape">
    <div class="bb-track-option is-active">
      <span>Existing tests</span>
      <strong>Add evidence to one flow</strong>
      <em>Use native Playwright, review one effect contract, and rerun until one flow is satisfied.</em>
      <b>Runtime path</b>
    </div>
    <div class="bb-track-option">
      <span>New behavior</span>
      <strong>Start from reviewed intent</strong>
      <em>Use Skills for EARS, Gherkin, Playwright, and effects before implementation repair.</em>
      <b>Spec path</b>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="bb-preflight" aria-label="Quickstart success criteria">
    <div class="bb-preflight-panel">
      <span>Start with</span>
      <strong>One runnable Playwright flow</strong>
      <p>You only need one stable flow ID and one effect contract proposal.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bb-preflight-panel is-success">
      <span>Stop at</span>
      <strong>One satisfied verdict</strong>
      <p>The first win is a reviewed behavior contract that passes against runtime evidence.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <article class="bb-track-panel is-active">
    <h2>Existing Tests: Add Runtime Evidence To One Flow</h2>
    <p>Use this path when you already have a system or E2E test that exercises a valuable flow. Keep the test. Add a stable flow tag and an effect contract.</p>

    <section>
      <h3><span aria-hidden="true">1</span>Declare the flow with native Playwright</h3>
      <p>Blackbox reads the <code>@flow</code> tag from <code>test.describe</code>. The ordinary Playwright assertion still checks the public result.</p>
      <Code code={flowSnippet} lang="ts" />
    </section>

    <section>
      <h3><span aria-hidden="true">2</span>Review one effect contract</h3>
      <p>Ask <code>$blackbox-effects</code> to propose required and forbidden effects from captured evidence, then review the exact YAML before accepting it.</p>
      <Code code={effectsSnippet} lang="yaml" />
      <Aside type="info" title="Effects Are Accepted Behavior">
        Keep effects that define correctness, remove incidental noise, and add
        forbids for behavior that would make the flow unsafe.
      </Aside>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h3><span aria-hidden="true">3</span>Rerun and read the verdict</h3>
      <p>Run <code>verify</code> without an update mode. The CLI writes runtime evidence and reports, not accepted behavior files.</p>
      <Code code={verifyCommand} lang="bash" />
      <Code code={verifyOutput} lang="json" />
    </section>
  </article>

  <section class="bb-after-success" aria-label="After first success">
    <div class="bb-after-success-head">
      <span>After first success</span>
      <h2 id="after-first-success">Choose how far to extend the harness</h2>
      <p>The first loop proves Blackbox can observe your system and enforce one reviewed effect contract.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="bb-next-signal">
      <a class="bb-next-primary" href="/docs/blackbox/quickstart/connect-specifications-to-runtime-evidence">
        <span class="bb-next-kicker">New behavior</span>
        <strong>Verify a Spec-Driven Feature</strong>
        <p>Take reviewed EARS requirements through Gherkin, native Playwright, runtime effects, and requirement verdicts.</p>
        <span class="bb-next-link">Open quickstart</span>
      </a>

      <details class="bb-next-command">
        <summary>Show command preview</summary>
        <Code code={featureCommands} lang="bash" />
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>
</section>

<style>
  .bb-quickstart {
    margin: 28px 0;
  }

  .bb-track-pick,
  .bb-preflight,
  .bb-next-signal {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 14px;
    margin: 20px 0;
  }

  .bb-track-option,
  .bb-preflight-panel,
  .bb-track-panel,
  .bb-after-success {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
  }

  .bb-track-option,
  .bb-preflight-panel {
    padding: 16px;
  }

  .bb-track-option.is-active,
  .bb-preflight-panel.is-success {
    border-color: rgba(96, 165, 250, 0.6);
    background: rgba(37, 99, 235, 0.12);
  }

  .bb-track-option span,
  .bb-preflight-panel span,
  .bb-after-success-head span,
  .bb-next-kicker {
    display: block;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 800;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  }

  .bb-track-option strong,
  .bb-preflight-panel strong,
  .bb-next-primary strong {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 4px;
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: 18px;
  }

  .bb-track-option em {
    display: block;
    margin: 8px 0 12px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-style: normal;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .bb-track-option b {
    color: #93c5fd;
    font-size: 13px;
  }

  .bb-track-panel,
  .bb-after-success {
    padding: 22px;
    margin-top: 22px;
  }

  .bb-track-panel h3 {
    display: flex;
    gap: 10px;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .bb-track-panel h3 span {
    display: inline-grid;
    width: 28px;
    height: 28px;
    place-items: center;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: #172554;
    color: #bfdbfe;
    font-size: 13px;
  }

  .bb-next-primary {
    display: block;
    padding: 18px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(96, 165, 250, 0.55);
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: rgba(37, 99, 235, 0.1);
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .bb-next-link {
    color: #93c5fd;
    font-weight: 800;
  }

  .bb-next-command {
    padding: 18px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 780px) {
    .bb-track-pick,
    .bb-preflight,
    .bb-next-signal {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
